A distributed decomposition of the RSBench OCR port in ../intel.

The lookup range is split into -r contiguous partitions, each with its own
producer chain and its own -b-wide sync batches, and the cross-section dataset
is generated in parallel by one task per nuclide and per material -- from the
same index-seeded value stream as ../intel, so the two describe the same
instance and the data is the same whatever the partitioning or the node count.
The per-nuclide pole and window counts are a histogram of one draw stream over
the whole nuclide index, so they cannot be produced per index: one pre-pass
task builds them and the per-nuclide generators consume them.  The dataset is summed into "RSBench pole checksum" and the
lookup results into "RSBench lookup checksum"; both are order-independent
integer sums.

To build and run

x86:
make -f Makefile.x86 clean run

x86-mpi:
make -f Makefile.x86-mpi clean run

Change the problem size WORKLOAD_ARGS argument
E.g.,
    make -f Makefile.x86 clean run WORKLOAD_ARGS="-d -s small -l 1000000 -r 64 -b 16"
